module

public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IntermediateField.Adjoin.Algebra
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FundamentalGroup.FiniteEtaleOverLimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Limits.AdjoinFinsetSystem
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# A scheme over a field base changed to an algebraic extension, as a limit of finite subextensions

Let `K` be a field, let `Kbar` be an algebraic extension of `K` — an algebraic closure, a
separable closure, or any algebraic extension — and let `X` be a quasi-compact and
quasi-separated scheme over `K`. This file presents the base change `X_{Kbar}` as a cofiltered
limit of the base changes `X_L` along the *finite* subextensions `K ⊆ L ⊆ Kbar`, in the form
required by the limit results for finite étale covers: the index category is cofiltered, the
transition morphisms are finite, and every stage is quasi-compact and quasi-separated. The
conclusion drawn is that every scheme finite étale over `X_{Kbar}` is the base change of one
finite étale over `X_L` for a single finite subextension `L`.

## The system

The limit presentation itself is `AlgebraicGeometry.AdjoinFinset.isLimitBcCone`, which holds for
an arbitrary ring map `K → Kbar`: the diagram is indexed by `(Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ`, the stage at `s`
being the base change of `X` along `Spec K[s] ⟶ Spec K` for `K[s] = Algebra.adjoin K s` the
`K`-subalgebra generated by `s`. What the hypothesis that `Kbar/K` is algebraic adds is that
these stages are the finite subextensions: `K[s]` is a field
(`AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.isField_adjoin`) finite over `K`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.moduleFinite_adjoin`), and it is the intermediate
field `K(s)` by `IntermediateField.adjoin_toSubalgebra`, so the index `s` names a finite
subextension `K ⊆ K(s) ⊆ Kbar` and every finite subextension is of this form.

## The hypotheses of the limit theorem

`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteEtale_model` asks for a cofiltered index category, affine
transition morphisms, and quasi-compact quasi-separated stages. Cofilteredness of
`(Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ` is automatic. The other two are supplied here from the hypothesis that
`Kbar/K` is algebraic, and *without* the Noetherian base and proper structure morphism that
`AlgebraicGeometry.AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram_compactSpace_and_quasiSeparatedSpace` asks for:

* `Spec K[s] ⟶ Spec K` is finite because `K[s]` is a finite `K`-module, so the stage projection
  `X_L ⟶ X` is finite as its base change, and a quasi-compact quasi-separated `X` therefore has
  quasi-compact quasi-separated stages above it.
* The transition `Spec K[s] ⟶ Spec K[t]` for `t ⊆ s` is finite because its composite with the
  finite `Spec K[t] ⟶ Spec K` is the finite `Spec K[s] ⟶ Spec K` and the former is separated.
  The transition `X_{K(s)} ⟶ X_{K(t)}` is its base change, hence finite, hence affine.

Finiteness of the transition morphisms is more than affineness, and it is what identifies the
system as a system of finite subextensions rather than merely of affine stages; affineness, which
is all the limit theorem consumes, is recorded separately as
`AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.isAffineHom_bcDiagram_map`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.stageToBase` — the projection `X_L ⟶ X` of a stage
  of the system down to `X`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.moduleFinite_adjoin`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.isField_adjoin` — the stage `K[s]` is a finite
  subextension of `Kbar/K`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.isFinite_stageToBase` — the stage projection
  `X_L ⟶ X` is finite.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.compactSpace_bcDiagram_obj` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.quasiSeparatedSpace_bcDiagram_obj` — the stages of
  a quasi-compact quasi-separated `X` are quasi-compact and quasi-separated.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.isFinite_bcDiagram_map` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.isAffineHom_bcDiagram_map` — the transition
  morphisms are finite, hence affine.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.exists_finiteEtale_model_of_isAlgebraic` — every
  scheme finite étale over `X_{Kbar}` is the base change of one finite étale over a stage `X_L`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.exists_finiteEtale_model_of_isAlgClosure` — the same
  for an algebraic closure, which is the case of a geometric fibre.

## Implementation notes

Mathlib's base-change functor `CategoryTheory.Over.pullback f` sends `Z ⟶ Spec K` to the second
projection of `Z ×_{Spec K} X`, so the stages are pullbacks with the `Spec` factor first, as in
`AlgebraicGeometry.AdjoinFinset.bcProj`. The statements below spell those pullbacks out rather
than writing them as `AlgebraicGeometry.AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram` applied to an index, so that a
consumer holding a cover of `X_{Kbar}` need not unfold the diagram to see that it applies;
`AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.stageToBase` carries the one defeq this relies on.

The transition morphisms are obtained as finite rather than merely affine by cancelling the
structure morphism to `Spec K` on the right, which is legitimate because a morphism of affine
schemes is separated, rather than by exhibiting the inclusion `K[t] ⊆ K[s]` as a module-finite
ring map: the latter would mean transporting the tower `K → K[t] → K[s]` across
`RingHom.toAlgebra`, since `RingHom.Finite` of the inclusion is stated for the algebra structure
that the inclusion itself induces and not for the one `K[s]` already carries.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BTV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BTV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BID](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BID)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace AlgebraicExtensionLimit

variable (K Kbar : Type u) [Field K] [Field Kbar] [Algebra K Kbar]

/-! ### The stages are the finite subextensions -/

section Subextension

variable [Algebra.IsAlgebraic K Kbar]

/-- **The subalgebra generated by a finite subset of an algebraic extension is finite.** Every
element of `Kbar` is integral over `K`, so `K[s]` is a finite `K`-module. -/
theorem moduleFinite_adjoin (s : Finset Kbar) :
    Module.Finite K (Algebra.adjoin K (s : Set Kbar)) :=
  Algebra.finite_adjoin_of_finite_of_isIntegral s.finite_toSet
    fun x _ ↦ (Algebra.IsAlgebraic.isAlgebraic (R := K) x).isIntegral

/-- The subalgebra `K[s]` of an algebraic extension is finite-dimensional over `K`. -/
theorem finiteDimensional_adjoin (s : Finset Kbar) :
    FiniteDimensional K (Algebra.adjoin K (s : Set Kbar)) :=
  moduleFinite_adjoin K Kbar s

/-- **The subalgebra `K[s]` of an algebraic extension is a field**, so that the stage indexed by
`s` is the base change along a finite subextension of `Kbar/K` and not merely along a finite
`K`-algebra. -/
theorem isField_adjoin (s : Finset Kbar) : IsField (Algebra.adjoin K (s : Set Kbar)) :=
  Subalgebra.isField_of_algebraic _

/-- **`Spec K[s] ⟶ Spec K` is finite**, because `K[s]` is a finite `K`-module. -/
theorem isFinite_specMap_algebraMap_adjoin (s : Finset Kbar) :
    IsFinite (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (algebraMap K (Algebra.adjoin K (s : Set Kbar))))) := by
  have := moduleFinite_adjoin K Kbar s
  rw [IsFinite.SpecMap_iff]
  exact RingHom.finite_algebraMap.mpr inferInstance

end Subextension

/-! ### The transition morphisms are finite -/

/-- **The transition morphisms of the system of subextensions are finite.** For `t ⊆ s` the
inclusion `K[t] ⊆ K[s]` makes `K[s]` a finite `K[t]`-module, read here by cancelling
`Spec K[t] ⟶ Spec K` — which is separated, being a morphism of affine schemes — on the right of
the finite morphism `Spec K[s] ⟶ Spec K`. -/
theorem isFinite_specDiagram_map [Algebra.IsAlgebraic K Kbar] {i j : (Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ}
    (e : i ⟶ j) : IsFinite ((AdjoinFinset.specDiagram K Kbar).map e) := by
  have hi : IsFinite ((AdjoinFinset.specToBase K Kbar).app i) :=
    isFinite_specMap_algebraMap_adjoin K Kbar i.unop
  have : IsSeparated ((AdjoinFinset.specToBase K Kbar).app j) :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsSeparated (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (algebraMap K (Algebra.adjoin K (j.unop : Set Kbar))))))
  have hnat : (AdjoinFinset.specDiagram K Kbar).map e ≫ (AdjoinFinset.specToBase K Kbar).app j
      = (AdjoinFinset.specToBase K Kbar).app i := by
    simp
  have : IsFinite ((AdjoinFinset.specDiagram K Kbar).map e ≫
      (AdjoinFinset.specToBase K Kbar).app j) := by rw [hnat]; exact hi
  exact IsFinite.of_comp ((AdjoinFinset.specDiagram K Kbar).map e)
    ((AdjoinFinset.specToBase K Kbar).app j)

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of K))

/-- **The transition morphisms of the system `{ X_{K(s)} }` are finite**, being base changes
along `f` of the finite transitions `Spec K[s] ⟶ Spec K[t]`. -/
theorem isFinite_bcDiagram_map [Algebra.IsAlgebraic K Kbar] {i j : (Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ} (e : i ⟶ j) :
    IsFinite ((AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram K Kbar f).map e) := by
  change IsFinite (((Over.pullback f).map ((AdjoinFinset.specOverDiagram K Kbar).map e)).left)
  refine MorphismProperty.overPullbackMap f ((AdjoinFinset.specOverDiagram K Kbar).map e) ?_
  change IsFinite ((AdjoinFinset.specDiagram K Kbar).map e)
  exact isFinite_specDiagram_map K Kbar e

/-- The transition morphisms of the system `{ X_{K(s)} }` are affine, which is the form in which
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteEtale_model` consumes them. -/
theorem isAffineHom_bcDiagram_map [Algebra.IsAlgebraic K Kbar] {i j : (Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ}
    (e : i ⟶ j) : IsAffineHom ((AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram K Kbar f).map e) :=
  have := isFinite_bcDiagram_map K Kbar f e
  inferInstance

/-! ### The stages are quasi-compact and quasi-separated -/

/-- The projection `X_{K(s)} ⟶ X` of a stage of the system down to `X`. It is the second
projection of the pullback defining the stage; the ascription here is the one place where that
description of the stage is matched against `AlgebraicGeometry.AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram`. -/
def stageToBase (i : (Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ) : (AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram K Kbar f).obj i ⟶ X :=
  pullback.snd (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
    (algebraMap K (Algebra.adjoin K (i.unop : Set Kbar))))) f

/-- **The stage projection `X_{K(s)} ⟶ X` is finite**, being the base change along `f` of the
finite morphism `Spec K[s] ⟶ Spec K`. -/
theorem isFinite_stageToBase [Algebra.IsAlgebraic K Kbar] (i : (Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ) :
    IsFinite (stageToBase K Kbar f i) := by
  have := isFinite_specMap_algebraMap_adjoin K Kbar i.unop
  exact inferInstanceAs (IsFinite (pullback.snd (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
    (algebraMap K (Algebra.adjoin K (i.unop : Set Kbar))))) f))

/-- **The stages of a quasi-compact `X` are quasi-compact**, because the stage projection
`X_{K(s)} ⟶ X` is finite, hence quasi-compact. -/
theorem compactSpace_bcDiagram_obj [Algebra.IsAlgebraic K Kbar] [CompactSpace X]
    (i : (Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ) : CompactSpace ((AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram K Kbar f).obj i) :=
  have := isFinite_stageToBase K Kbar f i
  QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (stageToBase K Kbar f i)

/-- **The stages of a quasi-separated `X` are quasi-separated**, because the stage projection
`X_{K(s)} ⟶ X` is finite, hence quasi-separated. -/
theorem quasiSeparatedSpace_bcDiagram_obj [Algebra.IsAlgebraic K Kbar] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (i : (Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ) : QuasiSeparatedSpace ((AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram K Kbar f).obj i) :=
  have := isFinite_stageToBase K Kbar f i
  quasiSeparatedSpace_of_quasiSeparated (stageToBase K Kbar f i)

/-! ### Finite étale covers of the base change to the algebraic extension -/

/-- **A finite étale cover of `X_{Kbar}` comes from a finite subextension.** Let `Kbar/K` be an
algebraic extension of fields and `X` a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme over `K`. Then
every scheme finite étale over `X_{Kbar}` is isomorphic, as a cover of `X_{Kbar}`, to the base
change along the projection of a scheme finite étale over `X_{K(s)}` for a single finite subset
`s` of `Kbar`, hence over the base change of `X` along a finite subextension of `Kbar/K`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteEtale_model` applied to the limit presentation
`AlgebraicGeometry.AdjoinFinset.isLimitBcCone`, whose hypotheses on the index category, the
transition morphisms and the stages are discharged by cofilteredness of `(Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.isAffineHom_bcDiagram_map`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.compactSpace_bcDiagram_obj` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.quasiSeparatedSpace_bcDiagram_obj`. -/
@[sga "4½ Arcata 5.2.6" "Clause b)"]
theorem exists_finiteEtale_model_of_isAlgebraic [Algebra.IsAlgebraic K Kbar] [CompactSpace X]
    [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (Y : FiniteEtaleOver (pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap K Kbar))) f)) :
    ∃ (s : Finset Kbar) (B : FiniteEtaleOver (pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (algebraMap K (Algebra.adjoin K (s : Set Kbar))))) f)),
      Nonempty (Y ≅
        (finiteEtaleBaseChange (AdjoinFinset.bcProj K Kbar f (Opposite.op s))).obj B) := by
  have : ∀ i, CompactSpace ((AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram K Kbar f).obj i) :=
    compactSpace_bcDiagram_obj K Kbar f
  have : ∀ i, QuasiSeparatedSpace ((AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram K Kbar f).obj i) :=
    quasiSeparatedSpace_bcDiagram_obj K Kbar f
  have : ∀ {i j : (Finset Kbar)ᵒᵖ} (e : i ⟶ j),
      IsAffineHom ((AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram K Kbar f).map e) := fun e ↦
    isAffineHom_bcDiagram_map K Kbar f e
  obtain ⟨i, B, hB⟩ := exists_finiteEtale_model (AdjoinFinset.bcDiagram K Kbar f)
    (AdjoinFinset.bcCone K Kbar f) (AdjoinFinset.isLimitBcCone K Kbar f) Y
  exact ⟨i.unop, B, hB⟩

/-- **A finite étale cover of a geometric fibre comes from a finite subextension.** The case of
`AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicExtensionLimit.exists_finiteEtale_model_of_isAlgebraic` in which
`Kbar` is an algebraic closure of `K`: for `X` quasi-compact and quasi-separated over `K`, every
scheme finite étale over `X_{Kbar}` is the base change of one finite étale over `X_{K(s)}` for a
single finite subset `s` of `Kbar`. -/
theorem exists_finiteEtale_model_of_isAlgClosure [IsAlgClosure K Kbar] [CompactSpace X]
    [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (Y : FiniteEtaleOver (pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap K Kbar))) f)) :
    ∃ (s : Finset Kbar) (B : FiniteEtaleOver (pullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (algebraMap K (Algebra.adjoin K (s : Set Kbar))))) f)),
      Nonempty (Y ≅
        (finiteEtaleBaseChange (AdjoinFinset.bcProj K Kbar f (Opposite.op s))).obj B) :=
  have : Algebra.IsAlgebraic K Kbar := IsAlgClosure.isAlgebraic
  exists_finiteEtale_model_of_isAlgebraic K Kbar f Y

end AlgebraicExtensionLimit

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
